  "method": "Independent stationary ON/OFF exponential trajectories sample the time to the first bright segment and its exposure-truncated duration. First-burst detection uses deterministic photons accrued in that segment. Independent unthinned Poisson labels are sampled uniformly in a square. Any active neighbor whose coordinates fall in the 250 nm disk counts as interference. Yield combines independent estimates of qualifying and clear-disk probabilities. Each check requires agreement within five null standard errors. Checks share component estimates.",
